//! Archive readers - `0x8019FE70..0x802BF9C0`.
//!
//! # What this module covers
//!
//! Two archive families share this file because they answer the same questions:
//! open a container, locate a member, and return that member's bytes and
//! length. The compressed-member path through both families ends in the two
//! Nintendo LZ routines at the bottom of the file.
//!
//! 1. **U8 / EGG archive helpers** - the file-info getters, member enumeration
//!    wrappers, and the EGG archive object (open/close/wait) that the resource
//!    registry ([`crate::resource::registry`]) drives. These live at
//!    `0x8019FE70..0x8019FE90` and `0x802B7830..0x802B7E50`.
//! 2. **NintendoWare sound-archive reader** - the reader object, header/index
//!    loaders, block decoder and buffer/stream cleanup at
//!    `0x8026F2D0..0x8026FF30`. It feeds [`crate::audio::seq`].
//! 3. **LZ decompression** - `0x801D8150`/`0x801D8190`, the header-size and
//!    back-reference expander used by `dres_get_res_compressed` and
//!    `dres_copy_res_compressed` in the registry.
//! 4. **RLYT header accessors and the default-record array** - the 24
//!    bitfield/copy accessors that the layout-header parser `0x802B20B0`
//!    calls while it walks a `.brlyt` member, the object's deleting
//!    destructor at `0x802B2BC0`, and the heap-backed 32-byte record array
//!    at `0x802B68B0..0x802B6A40`. These are recorded here because they read
//!    and write the same archive small-data band as the EGG root heap; no
//!    other module owns them. See the wave-46 section below.
//! 5. **Sound member-object classes and handle accessors** - the rest of the
//!    NW4R member-object family begun in wave 41: classes D..H at
//!    `0x8026B640..0x8026D330` (constructors, size queries, guard-mutex
//!    initialisers, release helpers, one manager-count dispatch and one
//!    deleting destructor), plus the field accessors at
//!    `0x80267300..0x802674D0`. Every constructor installs the same kind of
//!    vtable, clears the `+0x0C` active byte and copies an opaque default block
//!    from the `r2` small-data area. See the wave-49 section at the end.
//! 6. **`0x802B0000`-band size queries and entry accessors** - the packed-count
//!    section-offset family at `0x802B3300..0x802B35E0` (twelve bodies that
//!    combine the count word at `+0x38` with the base pointer at `+0x40`), the
//!    guarded entry getters at `0x802B5AF0..0x802B5CA0`, the ring-list
//!    membership test at `0x802BC230`, the child-object accessors at
//!    `0x802BC8C0..0x802BC920` and two flag getters at `0x802BF9B0`/
//!    `0x802BF9C0`. See the wave-54 section at the end. `// inferred:` the
//!    section table is layout/resource data; the exports prove only the
//!    arithmetic and the offsets.
//! 7. **Remaining `0x80260000`-band handle accessors and list helpers** - the
//!    float/byte accessors at `0x80265F40..0x80265FB0`, the wave-49 handle
//!    continuation at `0x80267390..0x802675F0`, the guarded-free and list
//!    cluster at `0x80267B40..0x80267D30`, and small field helpers at
//!    `0x802627E0..0x802666A0`. Twenty-eight bodies. See the wave-62 section
//!    at the end. `// inferred:` the owner is the same sound-handle record the
//!    wave-49 accessors write.
//! 8. **`0x802B0000`-band section-count writers and ordered-list nodes** - the
//!    five section-count setters at `0x802B3620..0x802B3940` (same `+0x38`
//!    count word, `+0x3C` bitfield and `+0x40` base pointer as item 6), the
//!    RLYT record initialiser at `0x802B2B50`, the entry-list release at
//!    `0x802B6320`, the byte scalers at `0x802B6AE0`/`0x802B6B50`, the colour
//!    forwarder at `0x802B71E0`, and the ordered queue behind the child object
//!    of [`fn_802bc920`] at `0x802BDB40..0x802BE450`. Twenty-seven bodies. See
//!    the wave-66 section at the end. `// inferred:` the queue is an NW4R
//!    intrusive list pair with the active list at `+0x04` and the free list at
//!    `+0x10`.
//! 9. **Last `0x80260000`-band deleters, accessors and one stream re-bind** -
//!    the `+0x00` word getter at `0x802610B0`, the fixed-layout descriptor
//!    initialiser at `0x80261D60`, six copies of the
//!    compiler-generated deleting destructor (`0x80261DB0`, `0x802654B0`,
//!    `0x802677A0`, `0x80267B80`, `0x80267BC0`, `0x80267C00`), the text writer
//!    at `0x802652E0..0x802653D0`, the pointer tests and forwarders at
//!    `0x80267700..0x80267760`, the entry-list drain at `0x80267DD0`, the
//!    clamped accumulator at `0x802688C0..0x80268900`, the `r2`-constant
//!    accessors at `0x802696F0..0x80269980`, the count getter at `0x8026A650`
//!    and the sibling-reader re-bind at `0x8026DE10`. Thirty bodies. See
//!    the wave-73 section at the end. `// inferred:` the records are NW4R
//!    sound/stream objects; the exports prove only the offsets, the masks and
//!    the callee addresses.
//! 10. **`0x802B0000`-band record copies, polygon getters and effect-object
//!     helpers** - the 2/4/16-byte record copies and the empty-list
//!     initialiser at `0x802B2070..0x802B2B10`, the `RLAN` section-table scan
//!     at `0x802B5B10`, the polygon-descriptor helpers behind the `+0x38`
//!     section table at `0x802B4C40..0x802B5E10`, the two-state flag setter
//!     and frame accumulator at `0x802BB0E0..0x802BB600`, the aligned buffer
//!     allocator at `0x802BC670`, and the effect-object getters and virtual
//!     `+0x08` getter copies at `0x802BC6E0..0x802BFF30`. Thirty bodies. See
//!     the wave-79 section at the end. `// inferred:` the owners are RLYT
//!     layout/polygon records plus one screen-effect object; the exports prove
//!     only the offsets, the tags and the callee addresses.
//! 11. **Remaining `0x80260000`-band sound state, list and range helpers** -
//!     the interrupt-masked handle stores at `0x80262200..0x802627C0`, the
//!     eleven-halfword block comparator and the two interleaved block copies at
//!     `0x80262FE0..0x80263810`, the `+0x30` mode selector, the three-list
//!     singleton and its descriptor insert/remove trio at
//!     `0x80264680..0x80265060`, the `RBKN` block decoder at `0x802656F0`, the
//!     two fixed field initialisers at `0x80265DB0`/`0x80265E80`, the `+0x88`
//!     mode test and counters at `0x802667D0..0x80266D80`, the `+0x10` virtual
