//! ## Yaz0 stream decoder (wave 24)
//!
//! The mount executor can route a compressed member through a stateful Yaz0
//! decoder instead of building a whole destination buffer first. The decoder
//! state is fed arbitrary source chunks and keeps its bit tag, match length and
//! back-distance between calls.
//!
//! | address | size | Rust | plain-English role |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | `0x802B85D0` | 48 B | [`lz_stream_init`] | initialise the decoder state |
//! | `0x802B8600` | 252 B | [`lz_stream_parse_header`] | verify `Yaz0` and read the size |
//! | `0x802B8700` | 620 B | [`lz_stream_decode`] | consume one source chunk |
//! | `0x802B8970` | 48 B | [`lz_stream_object_init`] | bind output buffer and size |
//! | `0x802B89A0` | 44 B | [`lz_stream_object_feed`] | feed a chunk, report completion |
//!
