//! ## Heap-object factories (wave 36)
//!
//! Wave 30 translated the allocator and the heap-list primitives but left the
//! concrete heap-object types and their factories as opaque addresses. This
//! pass supplies those at `0x802B8B40..0x802BA000`: the list initialiser, the
//! base constructor/destructor, the allocate/free trampolines that forward to
//! [`arc_heap_allocate`] / [`arc_heap_free`], and the four placement factories
//! that align a byte range, build the sub-heap through the `0x801Dxxxx`
//! helpers and publish the object through the `r13 - 0x484C` hook.
//!
//! | address | size | Rust | plain-English role |
//! |---|---|---|---:>
//! | `0x802B8B40` | 64 B | [`fn_802b8b40`] | initialise the heap list and mutex |
//! | `0x802B8B80` | 148 B | [`fn_802b8b80`] | construct the base heap object |
//! | `0x802B8C20` | 148 B | [`fn_802b8c20`] | destroy the base heap object |
//! | `0x802B9070` | 4 B | [`fn_802b9070`] | empty heap slot stub |
//! | `0x802B9080` | 228 B | [`fn_802b9080`] | report every live heap under the lock |
//! | `0x802B9210`/`0x802B9250` | 12 B | [`fn_802b9210`] | allocate `(size, 4, 0)` |
//! | `0x802B9220` | 8 B | [`fn_802b9220`] | return the second word |
//! | `0x802B9230`/`0x802B9260` | 8 B | [`fn_802b9230`] | allocate `(size, align, 0)` |
//! | `0x802B9240`/`0x802B9270` | 16 B | [`fn_802b9240`] | allocate `(size, align, heap)` |
//! | `0x802B9290` | 8 B | [`fn_802b9290`] | free through the thread heap |
