//! | `0x802B68B0` | 148 B | [`fn_802b68b0`] | grow the 32-byte record array |
//! | `0x802B6950` | 236 B | [`fn_802b6950`] | fill new records with defaults |
//! | `0x802B6A40` | 148 B | [`fn_802b6a40`] | copy records into the array |
//!
//! # Why this code exists in the image
//!
//! The sound reader is the disc-facing half of the NintendoWare sound library:
//! the `RSEQ` consumer in [`crate::audio::seq`] gets its bytes from blocks this
//! reader returns. `// inferred:` the container is NintendoWare's sound archive
//! (BRSAR, itself a U8-style archive); the functions never spell the format out,
//! so the identification rests on two facts:
//!
//! * the file is opened through the runtime file layer and keeps a 0x100-byte
//!   path plus a 0x30-byte file object, which is the shape of an archive handle,
//! * the index block at `+0x120`/`+0x124` and the stream length terms at
//!   `+0x170`/`+0x174` are exactly what a two-region archive needs.
//!
//! The value decoder is the strongest hint about the payload: its `width == 4`
//! arm expands a 16-bit random number into `[lo, hi]`, the idiom used for
//! randomised pitch/volume fields in sequence data.
//!
//! The U8 side is the member-table half of the resource registry: the registry
//! stores one EGG archive pointer per holder, calls the count/fill wrappers to
//! build `mpFiles`, and keeps the EGG archive object alive through the
//! `arc_object_*` lifecycle. Without these bodies the registry has to treat the
//! member table as opaque.
//!
//! ## U8 file-info block (offsets used here)
//!
//! `0x8019F9B0` fills one 12-byte record per member:
//!
//! | offset | meaning |
//! |---|---|
//! | `+0x00` | owning U8 handle |
//! | `+0x04` | member data offset (returned by [`arc_file_info_offset`]) |
//! | `+0x08` | member size (returned by [`arc_file_info_size`]) |
//!
//! ## EGG archive object (offsets used by the `arc_object_*` helpers)
//!
//! | offset | meaning (`// inferred:` from the stores/loads) |
//! |---|---|
//! | `+0x00` | vtable `0x8034FBE0` |
//! | `+0x04` | "entry open" byte |
//! | `+0x08` / `+0x20` | two OS mutexes |
//! | `+0x38` | counter cleared by [`arc_object_reset`] |
//! | `+0x3C` | DVD file-info block handed to `DVDFastOpen` |
//! | `+0x78` | back-pointer to the object |
//! | `+0x7C` / `+0x9C`, `+0xA0` / `+0xC0` | condition-variable pairs |
//! | `+0xC4` | word cleared before and after a wait |
//!
//! ## Reader object layout (offsets used here)
//!
//! | offset | meaning (`// inferred:` from the stores/loads) |
//! |---|---|
//! | `+0x008` | 0x100-byte stored path |
//! | `+0x018` | current stream offset, used by `0x8022AEF0` |
//! | `+0x108` | data-cursor sub-object; `+0x28` holds `buffer + 8` |
//! | `+0x118` / `+0x11C` | second block's file offset / size used by [`fn_8026fd00`] |
//! | `+0x120` / `+0x124` | index-block file offset / size |
//! | `+0x14C` | 0x30-byte file object handed to the runtime file layer |
//! | `+0x170` / `+0x174` | two length terms summed into the stream limit |
//! | `+0x1D8` | "file is open" byte |
//!
//! # Start here
//!
//! For the registry path, read [`arc_count_files`] → [`arc_get_file_array`] →
//! [`arc_object_open`]. For the sound path, read [`fn_8026f770`] first: it shows
//! the object layout, the file-layer calls and the two-buffer path normaliser.
//! Then [`fn_8026fc50`] and [`fn_8026fdb0`] show how blocks are fetched,
//! [`fn_8026f930`] closes the object, and [`fn_8026f2d0`] decodes what the
//! blocks contain.
//!
//! # Dependencies
//!
//! * [`crate::platform`] - big-endian volatile loads/stores and indirect calls.
//! * [`crate::resource::bres`] - the translated U8 directory walker
//!   `fn_802b7a40`, used by the two enumeration wrappers.
//! * [`crate::engine::startup::SDA_BASE`] - `r13`, needed for the lazy-init byte
//!   and header-size global in the sound reader.
//! * Local helper `call0_u32` - [`crate::platform::call0`] discards the return
//!   value, and the called routine's result is needed here.
//! * Callees outside this address range are called by absolute address and are
//!   **not** translated in this module: the runtime file layer (`0x801D8BD0`
//!   seek, `0x801D89F0` read, `0x801D95B0` open, `0x801D9850` close,
//!   `0x801DAA70` current directory), the DVD layer (`0x801CA990` fast open,
//!   `0x801CAA00` close, `0x801CAB20` synchronous read, `0x801CEE90` path
//!   probe), the EGG heap pair (`0x802B8CC0`, `0x802B8F70`), the cache
//!   invalidate `0x801AC440`, `VIWaitForRetrace` (`0x801BCCF0`), the path helpers
//!   `0x802756E0` / `0x80275CC0` / `0x80275ED0`, the streaming read
//!   `0x8022AEF0`, the cache write-back `0x801AC4A0`, the random generator
//!   `0x80283A30`, the two table lookups `0x80271CE0` / `0x80273DB0`, the
//!   NW4R list/mutex/condition helpers `0x80228DD0` / `0x80228DF0` /
//!   `0x80228F80` and `0x801B2390` / `0x801B24C0` / `0x801B2E20` /
//!   `0x801B2E60` / `0x801B2F40`, and the allocator `0x802B9280`.
//!
//! # Glossary (first use)
//!
//! * **DOL** - the Wii executable container `sys/main.dol`; addresses here are
//!   its *virtual* addresses (image base `0x80004000`), not file offsets.
//! * **U8 / RARC** - Nintendo's generic archive container (a header plus
//!   relative file entries). `// inferred:` BRSAR is built on the same idea.
//! * **EGG** - Nintendo's EGG library; its `Archive` object wraps a mounted U8
//!   handle and owns the member-search entry points.
//! * **BRSAR** - NintendoWare sound archive; the container this reader walks.
//! * **VLQ** - variable-length quantity: seven payload bits per byte with the
//!   high bit meaning "another byte follows"; used by `width == 3`.
//! * **EOF clamp** - reducing a read request so that `offset + len` stays inside
//!   the declared length, rounding up to a 32-byte boundary.
//! * **RSEQ** - the sound-sequence format consumed after these blocks are read;
//!   see [`crate::audio::seq`].
//!
//! # Status and provenance
//!
//! Five sound-reader functions were promoted from `src/subsystems/r80260_802ed.rs`
//! (ledger module `resource/archive`). Wave 7 added the 12 U8/EGG helpers, 10
//! further sound-reader bodies and the 2 LZ routines in place. Wave 15 added the
//! three EGG member-read bodies (`0x802B7ED0..0x802B8150`) and the U8 iterator
//! close (`0x801A0040`); wave 24 added the five Yaz0 stream bodies at
//! `0x802B85D0..0x802B89A0`; wave 30 added the eleven archive-heap bodies at
//! `0x802B8A70..0x802B9290`; wave 36 added the thirty heap-object factory bodies
//! at `0x802B8B40..0x802BA000`; wave 39 added the twenty-five DVD-reader,
//! buffer-cache and list-helper bodies at `0x80268C40..0x8026DE90`; wave 40
//! added the eighteen U8-member-table, LZ-binding and EGG-root-heap bodies at
//! `0x802B63B0..0x802BA870`; wave 41 added the twenty-eight sound-band
//! record-list and member-object bodies at `0x80260800..0x8026DB80`; wave 46
//! added the twenty-eight RLYT accessor and record-array bodies at
//! `0x802B2720..0x802B6A40`; wave 49 added the thirty remaining sound
//! member-object and handle-accessor bodies at `0x8026B640..0x8026D330` and
//! `0x80267300..0x802674D0`; wave 54 adds the twenty-eight size-query and
//! entry-accessor bodies at `0x802B3300..0x802BF9C0`; wave 62 added the
//! twenty-eight sound-band accessors at `0x802627E0..0x80267D30`; wave 66 added
//! the twenty-seven section-count, queue and record bodies at
//! `0x802B2B50..0x802BE450`; wave 73 added the thirty remaining sound-band
//! deleters, accessors and the sibling-reader re-bind at
//! `0x802610B0..0x8026DE10`, so with the later passes listed above the file
//! now owns 771 functions (747 ledgered plus 24 untabled aliases). Every body
//! keeps its `# Original` evidence block; none is a re-implementation. The
//! neighbouring slot-table functions live in [`crate::game::player`].
//! `// partial:` the four LZ completion tests at `0x802B8450..0x802B8570` omit
//! the decoder source/length arguments, which the Ghidra export does not show;
//! every other body is complete.

use crate::engine::startup::SDA_BASE;
use crate::platform;
use crate::resource::bres;

// ===========================================================================
// Archive-reader field offsets.
//
// The shipped image has no symbol table; every name below is a plain offset
// whose meaning is justified at the definition or marked `// inferred:`.
// ===========================================================================

/// Archive-reader object: 256-byte path buffer at `+0x08`.
const ARCHIVE_PATH: usize = 0x08;
/// Archive reader: sub-object used as a data cursor (`+0x28` holds the pointer).
const ARCHIVE_BLOCK: usize = 0x108;
/// Archive reader: 0x30-byte file object handed to the file layer.
const ARCHIVE_FILE: usize = 0x14C;
/// Archive reader: byte set to 1 while the file is open.
