//     the packed count word at `+0x38` and the base pointer at `+0x40`, then
//     returns the start of a sub-array as `base + sum(count * stride)`. The
//     strides are 0x1C (28-byte entries), 0x14 (20-byte entries) and 4 (word
//     entries). The exports show only the arithmetic, so the record meanings
//     stay `// unknown:`.
//   * `0x802B5AF0..0x802B5CA0` - a four-word clearer and five guarded getters
//     that defer to two child pointers at `+0x08` / `+0x0C` and return 0 when
//     the child is absent. `0x802B35E0` copies 0x14 bytes into `+0x44` and
//     clears `+0x58`; it is grouped with the size family because it shares the
//     same object.
