///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80262200` at `0x80262200` (152 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80262200_FUN_80262200.c`
/// - observed: `uVar1 = FUN_801b1140(); if (*param_1 == 0) { FUN_801b1180(); }
///   else { FUN_801b1140(); if (*param_1 == 0) { FUN_801b1180(); } else {
///   *(undefined2 *)(*param_1 + 0x96) = param_2; if ((*(uint *)(*param_1 +
///   0x1c) & 0x400) == 0) *(uint *)(*param_1 + 0x1c) |= 0x800;
///   FUN_801b1180(); } FUN_801b1180(uVar1); }`
/// - `// inferred:` the double disable/restore pair is the re-entrant guard the
///   sibling store helpers use; the export drops the restore masks.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: holder whose `+0x00` word is the live handle.
/// - `value`: halfword stored at handle `+0x96`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes the halfword and may set bit `0x800` in the handle's `+0x1C` flags.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be readable and, whenever `+0x00` is non-zero, that handle must
/// be writable through `+0x99`.
