// ===========================================================================
// Wave 97 - `0x80260000`-band sound-manager, stream and voice helpers
// (0x802605D0..0x8026DBA0)
//
// These bodies continue the NW4R sound band documented in the wave-49,
// wave-89 and wave-92 sections. Five groups share the same storage:
//
// - the sound-manager constructor at `0x802605D0` and its ready/list/tick
//   helpers at `0x80261190`/`0x80261BF0`;
// - the per-slot ramp stores at `0x80260A80`/`0x802610C0`/`0x80261B20`/
//   `0x802666C0`/`0x80267420`, all built on the linear-interpolation idiom
//   `low + cursor * (high - low) / duration`;
// - the note-cursor update at `0x80264220` and the two priority-queue
//   walkers at `0x80269B50`/`0x80269D00`;
// - the four voice-parameter commits at `0x8026BF40..0x8026D3B0`, which are
//   copies of one clamp-and-publish body over a ten/eleven-float input;
// - the sample-record loader at `0x80265B50`, the stream teardown pair at
//   `0x80268790`/`0x80268910` and the two envelope curves at
//   `0x80269740..0x80269990`;
// - the fractional clock advance at `0x8026DBA0`.
//
// Shared storage: the sound manager at `0x803FC810` with its ready byte at
// `r13 - 0x4994` and its inline list head at `0x803FC81C`; the stream list at
// `0x803FC958` with its ready byte at `r13 - 0x4978`; per-slot ramp records
// keeping `low`/`high` floats, `duration` and `cursor`. The exports print the
// CodeWarrior unsigned-int-to-double idiom as
// `CONCAT44(0x43300000, x ^ 0x80000000) - 2^52`; as in the wave-95 section it
// is written here as a plain `as f32`/`as f64` cast (see [`fn_802b4ae0`]).
//
