/// Pops the lowest-scored node from a priority queue under the buffer mutex.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80269b50` at `0x80269b50` (416 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80269b50_FUN_80269b50.c`
/// - observed: locks `FUN_8027b5f0() + 0x354` through `0x801b2e60`, computes a
///   `0..0x7F` score from `+0x98` and `+0x50`, walks the list at `+0x04` to
///   find the minimum score, refuses when the threshold is exceeded, runs the
///   winner's virtual `+0x10`, then links the list into `owner + 0x108`.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `list`: queue header; `+0x00` is the current budget, `+0x04` the head,
///   `+0x0C` the queued count.
/// - `owner`: sound record whose `+0x98` byte and `+0x50` word form the
///   threshold.
///
/// # Returns
/// `1` when a node was dispatched, `0` otherwise.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Locks/unlocks the buffer mutex, runs one virtual slot and relinks the list.
///
/// # Safety
/// The queue and every node must be valid; the winning node's vtable slot must
/// be callable.
///
/// # Confidence
