///   `0x802C3980` reads `f1` and `f2` before it writes either (`fsubs f4,f2,f1`
///   at `0x802C39B8`, `fneg f3,f1` at `0x802C39C0`), loads `f5` itself from
///   `r2 - 0x3D2C`, and overwrites `r4` from `r13 - 0x4780`, so no integer
///   argument beyond `this` survives to the callee.
