/// - observed: `lbzx` from `0x8042F318 + *(this+0x20)` supplies the record's
///   `+0x14` byte. `// unknown:` the forward direction stores a full word
///   from `0x8030D198` at `+0x20`, so the two tables only compose when that
///   word is a small byte offset; the instruction stream is unambiguous.
