///   else. The `1`/`2` arms test `*(r13 - 0x4744) == 1` (the saved viewport
///   word) and select the kind-1/kind-6 or the kind-27/kind-28 pane layout.
/// - observed: every pane extent comes from `fctiwz` of the geometry record's
///   `+0x08`/`+0x0C` pair, masked to sixteen bits.
/// - observed: mode 2's `+0x28` kind selects the `10`/`12`/`11`/`13` preset
///   numbers of `0x802C3020`; `+0x30` selects the extra pane kind and guards
///   the `0x802D3700`/`0x802C02C0` pair.
/// - Removed: the modelled `_savegpr_25` prologue call (`0x802DCD6C`) and the
///   two `_restgpr_25` epilogue calls (`0x802DCDB8`, one for the early
///   `+0x10` exit and one for the shared tail). The binary has a single
///   epilogue at `0x802C5F6C..0x802C5F80`; `this` is the incoming `r3` and
///   `mode` the incoming `r4`.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: live derived object whose `+0x04` primary vtable is
///   `0x803502A8`.
/// - `mode`: `0` state snapshot, `1` build, `2` teardown.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Allocates/destroys the `+0x1C`/`+0x20` child panes, rewrites the
/// `0x8042AED8` render-state word, programs GX state and calls one deferred
/// virtual slot at `+0x0C` of the window block.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be a live object of the family, the HUD owner and geometry
/// record behind `0x8042AED0` must be valid, and the window block produced by
/// `0x802D0830` must hold a usable vtable at `+0x28`.
