///   rows from `record + 0x14` (stride 4) to the `0x0C`-stride row array,
///   then loads `min(*(u16 *)(record + 0x10), *(byte *)(this + 0x04))` records
///   from `record + 0x48` (stride `0x50`) and copies the tint
///   `record + 0x34..0x37` to `this + 0x18..0x1B`.
/// - observed: the eight-times-unrolled copy that follows the mode-1 clamp is
///   unreachable in practice, because the same clamp caps the row count at
///   eight, so `r8 = count - 8 <= 0` always branches straight to the scalar
///   tail. The body below is that tail.
/// - observed, mode 2: loads `min(*(u16 *)(record + 0x10), *(byte *)(this +
///   0x06))` records from `record + 0x28` (stride `0x50`), copies the tint
///   `record + 0x14..0x17`, then copies `min(*(u16 *)(record + 0x12), *(byte *)
///   (this + 0x07))` packed `u32` rows from
///   `record + 0x28 + *(u16 *)(record + 0x10) * 0x50` (stride 8) into the row
///   array. `// observed:` the packed base uses the *unclamped* header count,
///   as the image does.
/// - observed: the two packed loops are the compiler's eight-times-unrolled
///   form (`bdnz` with a scalar tail); this body keeps the scalar copy, which
///   reproduces every store in the same order.
