///   `4e800020 bclr 20,0` - the body is the return instruction itself, so the
///   caller's `r3` is left untouched and no argument is read.
/// - extent: 4 bytes; twelve pad bytes follow up to `0x802CE850`.
/// - table evidence: the `+0x10` slot of [`VTABLE_80350444_A222`] and of the
///   `0x80350460` arc record that [`fn_802cef70`] installs - the same word
///   appears at `0x80350454` and `0x80350470`; the `0x80350480` record instead
///   overrides `+0x10` with [`fn_802cf760`].
///
/// # Arguments
/// None. The shipped virtual-call shape passes the object in `r3`; the slot is
