// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// `0x802D6640` - `0x80` size query with the `0x80278AB0` fallback
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Returns `0x80` when the sound-system probe has either of its two state words
/// set, otherwise tail-calls the seven-argument `0x80278AB0` fallback.
///
/// The probe is the BSS word at [`G_SOUND_PROBE_46E0`]. The body reads `+0x08`
/// first and answers `0x80` when it is non-zero; a zero `+0x08` then consults
/// `+0x04`, answering `0x80` on non-zero and falling back only when the whole
/// probe is null or both words are zero.
///
/// # Original (untabled)
/// - Ghidra: no export and no `functions.tsv` row for `0x802D6640`.
/// - Evidence: `work/dol/main.elf`, disassembly `0x802D6640..0x802D666F`:
///   `lwz r8,r13+0xffffb920`; `cmpi cr0,0,r8,0`; `bc 12,2` to the fallback;
///   `lwz r0,0x8(r8)`; `cmpi`; `bc 4,2` to `li r3,128`; `lwz r0,0x4(r8)`;
///   `cmpi`; `bc 12,2` to the fallback; `li r3,128`; `bclr 20,0`; the fallback
///   arm is `b 0x80278AB0`.
/// - extent: 48 bytes, `0x802D6640..0x802D6670`; the next body is the untabled
///   `0x802D6670` (`bclr`, then three zero words before `0x802D6680`).
/// - table evidence: word `0x80350774`, slot 13 of the `0x80350738`
///   construction vtable and slot 4 of the `0x8035075C` address point. The
///   sibling `0x8034F0E8` vtable binds the same role pair - slot 10
///   `0x8027A140` (`this - 0x0C` -> this body's target) and slot 13
///   `0x80278AB0` (`0x8034F124`) - so the fallback really is the class's
///   general loader.
/// - observed: `addi r3,r3,0` is absent, so the fallback receives the original
///   `r3..r9`; [`FN_80278AB0`] is documented to consume all seven.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: object receiving the query (`r3`).
/// - `argument1..argument6`: forwarded words `r4..r9`; they matter only on the
///   fallback path.
///
/// # Returns
/// `0x80` when the probe answers, else [`FN_80278AB0`]'s result.
///
/// # Side effects
/// The whole `0x80278AB0` path when the probe is absent.
///
/// # Safety
/// The probe must be readable when non-null, and the fallback callable.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high for the probe test and the `0x80` answer; medium for the fallback's
/// seven-word argument list, which is inferred from `0x80278AB0`'s prologue.
pub unsafe fn fn_802d6640(
    this: usize,
    argument1: u32,
    argument2: u32,
    argument3: u32,
    argument4: u32,
    argument5: u32,
    argument6: u32,
) -> u32 {
    let probe = platform::read_u32(G_SOUND_PROBE_46E0) as usize;
    if probe != 0
        && (platform::read_u32(probe + 0x08) != 0 || platform::read_u32(probe + 0x04) != 0)
    {
        return 0x80;
    }
    platform::call7(
        FN_80278AB0,
        this as u32,
        argument1,
        argument2,
        argument3,
        argument4,
        argument5,
        argument6,
    )
}

